      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "COLTRANE (1) broke last time so his manners can be a problem but he showed his talent with a win at this circuit and distance prior, drawing deep and working but proving too good by 9m. That took his strike rate here to 50 per cent. If he gets it right he should get every chance from the ace draw. TICTOK (4) is in good form with top-four finishes in her three starts since a win from the back line at Ballarat, most recently recording a second from this barrier. Should enjoy a nice run. Contender. I DREAM OF MILLIE (2) draws well and could be close to a win after finishing runner-up for the second time in a row last start, beaten 1.3 metres in the St Arnaud Cup. NAKEDTRUTH (10) has claims off a second from this barrier here last start while KYVALLEY MICHAEL NZ (8) draws for a trail and could be competitive.",
